Wave 1 Todo 3 release smoke

The executable scenario is replayed by:

    ./.omo/evidence/wave1-task3-arch-read-preview-cancel-smoke.sh

The script runs `target/release/packtide` with a temporary PATH containing only fake `pacman`, `paru`, `fzf`, and `sudo` commands. It never invokes a host package manager and does not use the host package database.

Observed scenarios:

    PACKTIDE_INSTALL_LIST_ONLY=1 target/release/packtide install
    target/release/packtide __preview install $'core\tbash\t5.3-1'
    target/release/packtide install
    target/release/packtide install        # with both paru and yay absent

The captured release-binary output and exit statuses are in `wave1-task3-arch-read-preview-cancel-smoke.log`:

    read.list.status=0
    preview.status=0
    cancel.status=0
    missing_helper.status=1
    assertions.no_sudo=true
    assertions.no_transaction=true
    cleanup.fixture_exists_after_cleanup=false

The fake `fzf` returns status 1 and captures the read rows, so cancellation reaches the normal localized cancellation result without invoking the fake transaction helper. The fake `sudo` marker is absent for list/read, preview, cancellation, and the missing-helper capability error. No install, remove, upgrade, or other real transaction was run.
